  "description": "The \u0027dss_plugins_cached\u0027 dataset provides a comprehensive overview of various plugins, capturing essential details such as unique identifiers, human-readable names, version numbers, and authorship. This dataset is particularly useful for developers and administrators managing plugin libraries, as it facilitates easy reference and identification of plugins. Each entry includes a unique ID, a label for easy recognition, and a version number to track updates and changes. The dataset also includes the author\u0027s information, which is crucial for understanding the source and credibility of the plugin. Tags are provided to categorize plugins, aiding in efficient search and filtering. Additionally, a detailed description of each plugin\u0027s functionality and use cases is included, offering insights into its applications. The \u0027isDev\u0027 column indicates whether a plugin is still in development, which is vital for status tracking and deployment decisions. Finally, a URL is provided for each plugin, linking to a summary page for more detailed information. This dataset is an invaluable resource for managing and utilizing plugins effectively within a software environment.",
